<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Helium-3. Suggestion 2.4.

  The Barrens exist for what is under them, and nothing in the mod produced it. This
  is the export: a canistered gas that the Society buys for standing (census caravan,
  TraderKindDefs/TraderKinds_RimRising.xml) and the merchant houses buy for silver.

  OBTAINED BY DEEP DRILLING. The three deep* fields below are what vanilla's own deep
  resources (Uranium, Plasteel in Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Resource_Stuff.xml)
  carry. UNVERIFIED FROM HERE: no reference mod on GitHub defines a deep resource, so
  these three names come from memory of the vanilla file and must be checked against
  it before this is called done - Find-VanillaDef.ps1 -Contains deepCommonality. If
  a name is wrong the game logs an XML field error naming this def on load.

  Deep resources are global, so a scanner on any map can find helium. That is
  accepted: the Barrens' claim is that the seam is RICH there, which the clawDrill
  (ThingDefs_Buildings/Buildings_RimRising.xml) expresses by yielding more of it.

  Everything else mirrored from RR_Ionsteel in Items_Resource_RimRising.xml, which was
  itself mirrored from vanilla's ComponentIndustrial.

  PULSE ARMOUR UPKEEP IS DELIBERATELY NOT DONE. The suggestion flags that fuel on
  clothing is disliked; the honest middle path (the trauma suite restocking from
  helium) is a C# change in TraumaSuite.cs and is listed in docs/Opus-Notes.md as a
  design call for the user first.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RR_HeliumThree</defName>
    <label>helium-3</label>
    <description>A pressurised canister of the isotope the whole Society runs on: the fuel for its reactors, its warships and its claim on everything else. It comes up out of the ground in a few places, and the people who bring it up are not the ones who are paid for it.\n\nOne canister will not light a room. A thousand will move a fleet.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RR_HeliumThree</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <soundInteract>Metal_Drop</soundInteract>
    <soundDrop>Standard_Drop</soundDrop>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <healthAffectsPrice>false</healthAffectsPrice>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
      <!-- Between plasteel (9) and uranium (6) per unit is too cheap for a fuel the
           Society wages wars over; this sits at uranium x4 so a stack is worth a trip. -->
      <MarketValue>24</MarketValue>
      <!-- Favour from a census caravan, at vanilla gold's rate: 0.015 per 10 silver. -->
      <RoyalFavorValue>0.036</RoyalFavorValue>
      <Mass>0.6</Mass>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>0.5</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <tradeTags>
      <!-- What the census caravan buys. See TraderKinds_RimRising.xml. -->
      <li>RR_SocietyTribute</li>
    </tradeTags>
    <!-- VERIFY these three against Items_Resource_Stuff.xml (Uranium). -->
    <deepCommonality>0.6</deepCommonality>
    <deepCountPerPortion>8</deepCountPerPortion>
    <deepLumpSizeRange>6~18</deepLumpSizeRange>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
